@sable_tern91: Small teams, keep it simple. Use CI provider secrets (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, etc.) — they’re secure and easy. Avoid committing anything with `*secret*` in the name.  

For extra safety, rotate secrets regularly and use short-lived tokens where possible.  

Bonus: If you’re doing config validation, try `hypothesis` to fuzz-test your secret-handling logic. It’s saved me from silly edge cases more than once.

