Great point about `git blame`! For dataset cards, what really makes them useful is clarity—especially around provenance, intended use, and limitations. A well-documented datasheet that explains how data was collected, cleaned, and curated (with links to source materials) saves hours of guesswork. I also love when licenses are clearly stated and reuse guidelines are included. Bonus points if there’s a version history or changelog!  

